ommended\\\\\\\\n  - Custom attributes for user roles\\\\\\\\n- **Identity Pool**: For AWS credential management\\\\\\\\n- **App Client**: For frontend authentication flow\\\\\\\\n- **Lambda Triggers**: Pre-authentication and post-confirmation\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Amazon SES Integration\\\\\\\\n- **Verified Domain**: HOA's domain for sending emails\\\\\\\\n- **Email Templates**:\\\\\\\\n  - Contact form notification template\\\\\\\\n  - User registration confirmation\\\\\\\\n  - Password reset template\\\\\\\\n- **Configuration Set**: For tracking email metrics\\\\\\\\n- **SNS Topic**: For bounce/complaint handling\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Additional Integrations\\\\\\\\n- **S3 Bucket**: For storing protected documents and news images\\\\\\\\n  - Bucket policies for access control\\\\\\\\n  - Lifecycle policies for cost optimization\\\\\\\\n  - CloudFront distribution for content delivery\\\\\\\\n- **CloudWatch**: Comprehensive logging and monitoring\\\\\\\\n- **AWS Secrets Manager**: For storing API keys and sensitive configuration\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Implementation Considerations\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Security Best Practices\\\\\\\\n- All endpoints use HTTPS\\\\\\\\n- API Gateway request throttling\\\\\\\\n- WAF rules for common attacks\\\\\\\\n- Regular security audits\\\\\\\\n- Principle of least privilege for all IAM roles\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Performance Optimization\\\\\\\\n- Lambda function warming for critical endpoints\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB auto-scaling policies\\\\\\\\n- API Gateway caching for read operations\\\\\\\\n- CloudFront CDN for static assets\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Cost Optimization\\\\\\\\n- Serverless architecture ensures pay-per-use\\\\\\\\n- DynamoDB on-demand pricing\\\\\\\\n- S3 lifecycle policies\\\\\\\\n- Lambda reserved concurrency only where needed\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### User Management Simplification\\\\\\\\n- Simple web-based admin panel for content management\\\\\\\\n- WYSIWYG editor for news/events creation\\\\\\\\n- Drag-and-drop file upload for documents\\\\\\\\n- Email notifications for new submissions\\\\\\\\n- Role-based access control (Admin, Editor, Viewer)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Deployment Strategy\\\\\\\\n1. Create DynamoDB tables with proper indexes\\\\\\\\n2. Set up Cognito User and Identity Pools\\\\\\\\n3. Configure SES with domain verification\\\\\\\\n4. Deploy Lambda functions with environment variables\\\\\\\\n5. Create API Gateway with all endpoints\\\\\\\\n6. Configure API Gateway authorizers with Cognito\\\\\\\\n7. Set up CloudWatch alarms and dashboards\\\\\\\\n8. Create S3 buckets with proper policies\\\\\\\\n9. Test all endpoints thoroughly\\\\\\\\n10. Document API for frontend integration\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis architecture provides a robust, scalable, and maintainable backend that meets all requirements while remaining simple for non-technical users to manage content through a user-friendly interface.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order-frontend-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order frontend-plan-1 from agent 4: Chief Delta,\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI have received and analyzed your orders regarding the frontend plan for the HOA website. My approach is to establish a high-level strategy and delegate the detailed planning to a team of specialized Supervisors. Here is the outline of the plan, which will be further developed by these new subordinates:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1.  **Framework & Architecture:** We will use **React** with the **Vite** build tool for a modern, performant, and developer-friendly foundation. The architecture will be component-based, organized into distinct directories for pages, shared components, layouts, services, and hooks. Routing will be handled by **React Router**. For state management, we will employ a global state solution like **Zustand** or **Redux Toolkit** to manage user session data and other application-wide state. I am recruiting 